   "2"
  ],
  "note": "NVIDIA's llama.cpp fork (brianchmielNV/llama.cpp @ 98a74c97, the build the model card gives) on NVIDIA's Q5_K_M GGUF (nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-Labs-Dory1.0-4B-GGUF @ 0963c80, sha256 96080be4...). -c 32768 -np 1, -ngl 999, -b 2048, -lm none (weights count in phys_footprint), prompt cache at --cache-ram 8192, --min-p 0, the GGUF's own chat template (--jinja), loops and KV mode by --override-kv as the card shows. Flash attention on and -ub 2048: its fastest reading and writing in a sweep (4K prompt, 2 loops, last-loop: -fa on -ub 2048 450 tok/s and 6.1 tok/s; -fa off 409-427 and 5.4-5.6). It writes about 6 tok/s, so its decode runs are 2 x 256 tokens (bench_args).",
